  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Herringbone works between two parallel guide lines. Each stitch travels diagonally to one line, makes a small backward step along it, then crosses diagonally to the other line and steps back there. The alternating direction of travel creates the X crossings that give the stitch its woven look.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What you need",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Thread",
              "value": "Stranded cotton, 2 strands"
            },
            {
              "label": "Fabric",
              "value": "Cotton or linen"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needle",
              "value": "Embroidery needle size 9"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hoop",
              "value": "15 cm embroidery hoop"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Working a practice row",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Draw two parallel lines about 8 mm apart. Bring the needle up at the bottom-left.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Insert at the top line, 8 mm to the right. Bring up 3 mm to the left on the top line.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Insert at the bottom line, 8 mm to the right of where you started. Bring up 3 mm to the left on the bottom line.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Continue in this zigzag rhythm. Each stitch crosses the previous one at the guide lines.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Common mistakes",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "intro": "Two common problems.",
          "items": [
            {
              "fix": "Keep the backward step the same length every time: 2 to 3 mm.",
              "cause": "The backward step on each line is not consistent.",
              "symptom": "The crossings are uneven"
            },
            {
              "fix": "Use two parallel lines at least 8 mm apart and keep forward spacing at 6 to 8 mm.",
              "cause": "Guide lines are too close together or spacing between stitches is too wide.",
              "symptom": "The angles are too shallow and the pattern looks flat"
            }
          ],
          "heading": "When herringbone goes wrong"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Uses and related stitches"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Herringbone stitch forms the base for interlaced herringbone, where a second thread is woven through the crossings without entering the fabric. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Closed herringbone",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "techniqueLink",
                "attrs": {
                  "techniqueSlug": "embroidery-closed-herringbone-stitch",
                  "label": "Closed herringbone"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " (with no step) is a seam stitch and the basis of shadow work."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
